"Arthur J. O'Dwyer" <ajo@nospam.andrew.cmu.edu> writes:
>   Right.  IOW, you can't kill a monster wearing an "AoLS without the
> "AoLS kicking in.  This should be obvious in hindsight, shouldn't it? ;)
> 
>   So, how can you get monsters to drop or give up things without
> killing them?  AFAIK, stealing is the only way.  But source divers
> alert!: are there any monsters that cannot wear amulets?  What happens
> if you polymorph the orc into one of them (if they exist)?

Polymorphing a monster wearing an AoLS will result in it continuing to
wear that AoLS, even if it would have been unable to put the amulet on
in that form.

However, the above said, polymorphing can still help; if you polymorph
a monster into a non-living form (undead, golems, vortices), the
amulet won't kick in (since it doesn't have any life to save) and so
you can grab it once you've destroyed the monster. Anything you
"destroy" rather than "kill".

